{"agreement":{"agreement_key":"jarr-clitic-li-majrur-visible-kasra","compared_fields":["conclusion","reason_key"],"conclusion_agrees":true,"gloss_text_used_for_agreement":false,"reason_agrees":true},"artifact_id":"two-vote-artifact:quran_12_31_24:p00slice-li-jarr","claim_state":"two_vote_verified","claimed_decision_state":"two_vote","occurrence":{"quran_loc":"quran:12:31:24","surface":"لِلَّهِ","wbw_loc":"wbw:12:31:24"},"reclassification":null,"schema":"qamus.two_vote_artifact.v1.1","votes":[{"conclusion":{"attachment":"muta-alliq-to-exclamative","attachment_key":null,"case_or_mood":{"mood_basis":"governed","sign":"kasra","sign_visibility":"visible","value":"jarr"},"contextual_function":"jarr-clitic-li-preposition-on-noun-host","function":"harf-jarr-lam-fused","governed_expression":"الله","governor":{"loc":"quran:12:31:23","relation":"muta-alliq","surface":"حاش"},"referent":null},"form":null,"gloss":"for Allah (exclamation of His transcendence)","grammatical_reason":"MCP iʿrāb verbatim: (اللَّامُ) حَرْفُ جَرٍّ مَبْنِيٌّ عَلَى الْكَسْرِ، وَاسْمُ الْجَلَالَةِ اسْمٌ مَجْرُورٌ وَعَلَامَةُ جَرِّهِ الْكَسْرَةُ الظَّاهِرَةُ. The phrase completes the exclamative حاش (tanzih) in حاش لله. Fused rasm: alif al-wasl of الله elided after the clitic (MCP rasm_note).","lexical_identity":{"entry_id":"b10a1ee04666","lemma_ar":"لِـ"},"lexical_target":"clitic_entry","occurrence":{"quran_loc":"quran:12:31:24","surface":"لِلَّهِ","wbw_loc":"wbw:12:31:24"},"reason_key":"jarr-clitic-li-majrur-visible-kasra","reviewer":{"engine":"claude-code-flagship-lane","lane":"reviewer-a","model":"claude-fable-5","reviewer_id":"reviewer-a-flagship-lane-20260728"},"root":null,"segmentation":[{"role":"jarr_clitic_lam","segment_surface":"لِ"},{"role":"proper_name_majrur","segment_surface":"لَّهِ"}],"timestamp":"2026-07-28T18:00:00Z","unresolved_points":["hasha analysis rivalry: حاش read as exclamative harf/verb of tanzih; taalluq of the jarr-phrase is one standard reading"],"vote_id":"vote:reviewer-a:12_31_24:p00slice:20260728"},{"conclusion":{"attachment":"muta-alliq-to-exclamative","attachment_key":null,"case_or_mood":{"mood_basis":"governed","sign":"kasra","sign_visibility":"visible","value":"jarr"},"contextual_function":"jarr-clitic-li-preposition-on-noun-host","function":"harf-jarr-lam-fused","governed_expression":"الله","governor":{"loc":"quran:12:31:23","relation":"muta-alliq","surface":"حاش"},"referent":null},"form":null,"gloss":"(exoneration) of/for Allah — 'Allah forbid!'","grammatical_reason":"MCP irab (markaz): «(اللَّامُ) حَرْفُ جَرٍّ مَبْنِيٌّ عَلَى الْكَسْرِ، وَاسْمُ الْجَلَالَةِ اسْمٌ مَجْرُورٌ وَعَلَامَةُ جَرِّهِ الْكَسْرَةُ الظَّاهِرَةُ». Context: قلن حاش لله — the exclamatory tanzih formula. The lam is the jarr clitic li- fused onto lafz al-jalala (wasla alif elided per rasm_note); the jarr-phrase attaches to the exclamative حاش (whether حاش is parsed as a frozen tanzih verb or as an ism masdar, it is the muta'alliq). Host is the proper name الله, madda (أله); kasra visible. Some grammarians treat this lam as zaʾida lil-bayan — noted below.","lexical_identity":{"entry_id":"b10a1ee04666","lemma_ar":"لِـ"},"lexical_target":"clitic_entry","occurrence":{"quran_loc":"quran:12:31:24","surface":"لِلَّهِ","wbw_loc":"wbw:12:31:24"},"reason_key":"jarr-clitic-li-majrur-visible-kasra","reviewer":{"engine":"claude-agent-subprocess-independent-lane","lane":"reviewer-b","model":"claude-fable-5","reviewer_id":"reviewer-b-independent-lane-20260728"},"root":null,"segmentation":[{"role":"jarr_clitic_lam","segment_surface":"لِ"},{"role":"proper_name_majrur","segment_surface":"لَّهِ"}],"timestamp":"2026-07-28T19:00:00Z","unresolved_points":["Rival classical analysis treats حاش itself as a jarr particle with the lam as lam zaʾida (bayan/taʿajjub); I conclude حاش is the exclamative muta'alliq and the lam is the ordinary jarr clitic, but the zaʾida reading would leave the phrase without a true muta'alliq.","Attachment value muta-alliq-to-exclamative chosen over muta-alliq-to-verb: حاش is verb-like for those who parse it as فعل ماض جامد; the menu separates the two and the exclamative reading is my winner."],"vote_id":"vote:reviewer-b:12_31_24:p00slice:20260728"}],"votes_fabricated":false}
